**Security Implications:**
- If someone knows the port is 3000, they can attempt attacks on that specific port
- Cannot deploy to different environments (dev, staging, prod) effectively
- Container/compose configurations become less flexible

**Recommended Fix:**
```javascript
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
const HOST = process.env.HOST || '0.0.0.0';

app.listen(PORT, HOST, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on ${process.env.HOST || '0.0.0.0'}:${PORT}`);
});
